        "stem": "A machine gives $y=(5x+7)/3$. Its second display originally reads $z=(2y+4)/5$. The input x increases by 9, and at the same time the second-display formula is replaced by $(2y-k)/5$. The reading of the second display is unchanged. Which option makes x the subject of the ORIGINAL z formula and gives k?",
